  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "critical",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Manual validation only; scripts could not be run in this environment. Present inherent risk is critical because an untrusted ticket reaches S3 capabilities: MFA reset under shared service authority and irreversible delivery of a temporary pass to the ticket requester. Residual remains critical because the only declared preventive control is a high-volume raw-action approval gate on cap.mfa_reset, and the design still sends the temporary pass to whoever opened the ticket rather than a verified account owner. Forecast remains critical because removal or weakening of the approval gate does not create the main weakness; the core design flaw is missing structural recipient binding and identity verification."
